WHY APACHE-2.0

Apache-2.0 was chosen over MIT for two reasons that matter for software that
touches people's money:

  * Section 7 (Disclaimer of Warranty) and Section 8 (Limitation of Liability)
    are explicit and detailed, where MIT's equivalent is one sentence. For a
    tool that outputs portfolio analytics, a clearly worded disclaimer of
    liability is worth having.
  * Section 3 grants an express patent licence and terminates it for anyone who
    brings a patent suit over the work.

If you would rather keep this proprietary — for example to commercialise it
exclusively — replace LICENSE with your own terms before publishing. Once a
permissive licence has been published for a given commit, it cannot be revoked
for that commit.

